parse_wkb_multilinestring/multipolygon: reject NULL child members

A corrupted WKB child inside a MultiLineString can be linestring-typed yet
carry a NULL tg_line (same for polygon-typed children of a MultiPolygon and
tg_poly). The parser stored the NULL member in the multi geometry, and any
consumer that assumes members are non-NULL — the WKT writer, for one —
then dereferences NULL.

Treat a NULL member as an invalid child at parse time, the same way a
wrongly-typed child is rejected.

Found by fuzzing WKB inputs through sqlite-tg; reachable from any WKB
parse entry point (tg_parse_wkb and friends).

diff --git a/tg.c b/tg.c
--- a/tg.c
+++ b/tg.c
@@ -12611,7 +12611,15 @@ static size_t parse_wkb_multilinestring(const uint8_t *wkb, size_t len,
             gerr = make_parse_error(wkb_invalid_child_type());
             goto fail;
         }
-        struct tg_line *line = tg_line_clone(tg_geom_line(child));
+        // PATCH(sqlite-tg): a corrupted WKB child can be linestring-typed yet
+        // carry a NULL line; upstream stores it and every consumer that
+        // assumes a non-NULL member (e.g. the WKT writer) then derefs NULL.
+        const struct tg_line *cline = tg_geom_line(child);
+        if (!cline) {
+            gerr = make_parse_error(wkb_invalid_child_type());
+            goto fail;
+        }
+        struct tg_line *line = tg_line_clone(cline);
         if (!lvec_append(&lines, line)) {
             tg_line_free(line);
             goto fail;
@@ -12692,7 +12700,15 @@ static size_t parse_wkb_multipolygon(const uint8_t *wkb, size_t len,
             gerr = make_parse_error(wkb_invalid_child_type());
             goto fail;
         }
-        struct tg_poly *poly = tg_poly_clone(tg_geom_poly(child));
+        // PATCH(sqlite-tg): see the multilinestring parser above — reject a
+        // polygon-typed child that carries a NULL poly rather than letting a
+        // NULL member reach the writer and other consumers.
+        const struct tg_poly *cpoly = tg_geom_poly(child);
+        if (!cpoly) {
+            gerr = make_parse_error(wkb_invalid_child_type());
+            goto fail;
+        }
+        struct tg_poly *poly = tg_poly_clone(cpoly);
         if (!pvec_append(&polys, poly)) {
             tg_poly_free(poly);
             goto fail;
